  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "OpenCode Bridge",
      "text": "[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-opencode-bridge)\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-opencode-bridge)\n[](LICENSE)\n[](https://github.com/Vikrant-Aleph/dsh-opencode-bridge/releases/latest)\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-opencode-bridge)\n\n[中文](README.zh.md) | English"
    },
    {
      "section": "OpenCode Bridge",
      "text": "A plugin for using [OpenCode](https://opencode.ai) free models in\n[DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) (DSH).\nNo OpenCode account or API key is required by default. Supports automatic model\nrefresh, optional context trimming of completed-turn reasoning,\nand egress-proxy rotation, with a fail-closed tool bridge and offline agent-scoped auditing."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **Automatic model refresh**: fetches the free-model list at startup and every 10 minutes by default, adds/removes models as the upstream catalog changes, and retains the last successful list if a refresh fails.\n- **Optional context trimming**: clear only confirmed completed-turn reasoning, retain the current tool chain, and keep full replay by default.\n- **Streaming and tool calls**: preserves reasoning history across multi-step tool calls, adapts DSH's native tools, and rejects unverified conversions rather than treating Bash commands as PowerShell.\n- **Optional proxy failover**: configure multiple HTTP(S) or SOCKS proxies, try another ready egress for explicit egress-quota errors or connection failures, and respect server-requested waits."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install and get started",
      "text": "Image input requires DSH's attachment request-version API; this version is built and verified against DSH SDK 0.2.1-rc.2."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install in DSH Desktop",
      "text": "1. Open **Plugins** in the sidebar, then click **Add plugin** in the top-right corner.\n2. Enter:\n\n```text\n   dsh-opencode-bridge@0.5.5\n   ```\n\n3. Prefer the official npm registry under **Installation source**. Mirrors may take time to sync new versions.\n4. Click **Install** and wait for completion."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install from the command line",
      "text": "Install from npm into your DSH profile:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile desktop add dsh-opencode-bridge@0.5.5\n```\n\nReplace `desktop` with the profile you use. If `dsh` is not available in your terminal, use:\n\n```sh\nnpx @deepseek-ai/dsh plugin --profile desktop add dsh-opencode-bridge@0.5.5\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install from the command line",
      "text": "After installation, select a model under **OpenCode Bridge** in the model picker. If it does not appear, restart the corresponding DSH profile.\nNormal use requires no API key or manual configuration-file edits. List changes are announced to DSH's model picker without restarting the plugin. Advanced refresh-interval configuration is documented in the [configuration reference](TECHNICAL.md#8-configuration-reference)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Optional context trimming",
      "text": "Open **Settings → OpenCode Bridge → Context trimming** to enable **Trim reasoning from completed turns**. It is off by default (full replay). Only reasoning from confirmed successful completed turns is cleared; the current tool chain and uncertain/interrupted history remain intact. Required `reasoning_content` fields are still sent."
    },
    {
      "section": "Optional context trimming",
      "text": "The setting is saved through DSH and applies to new requests without deleting local history or interrupting running requests. Savings depend on the upstream; DSH's local estimate may still include full history. Turn it off if continuity is affected."
    },
    {
      "section": "Optional proxy setup",
      "text": "Without proxy configuration, the plugin uses a direct connection from your machine.\n\n1. Open **Settings → OpenCode Bridge → Egress rotation (optional)**.\n2. Add your existing proxy addresses one at a time, such as `http://127.0.0.1:7890` or `socks5h://127.0.0.1:1080`. You can keep `direct` (this machine) as an egress.\n3. Use **Test all** to check connectivity. Cooling entries are skipped to avoid early requests. Adding or removing an entry saves and applies the change automatically."
    },
    {
      "section": "Optional proxy setup",
      "text": "The plugin prefers ready entries in list order. Explicit egress-quota errors or connection failures temporarily cool an entry. A server-requested wait prevents immediate failover, and a fully cooling pool sends no early requests. Model-backend unavailability and unexplained 429s are not automatically treated as exhausted proxy quota."
    },
    {
      "section": "Optional proxy setup",
      "text": "DSH centrally performs at most two automatic retries; excessive waits return an error for you to retry later. Replies that have started streaming are not automatically replayed.\n\n**HTTP(S), SOCKS4/4a and SOCKS5/5h** proxies are supported. Use only authorized proxies and respect upstream service limits."
    },
    {
      "section": "Important notes",
      "text": "- **Unofficial project**: not affiliated with OpenCode or DeepSeek. Upstream protocols, models and free quotas may change; continued availability is not guaranteed.\n- **Third-party processing**: model requests are sent to OpenCode's service and, when configured, traverse your proxy. Do not send content you would not entrust to those third parties.\n- **Attachments**: image input follows each model's declared capability. DSH prepares request versions and applies image budgets/offload decisions; ordinary files remain text handles rather than native file inputs. Image bytes and data URLs are not written to diagnostic logs.\n- **Credentials and logs**: proxy passwords are stored in plaintext locally. SOCKS username/password authentication is not encrypted by SOCKS itself; use trusted proxies and networks. Do not publish the configuration file; inspect logs and screenshots for sensitive information before sharing."
    },
    {
      "section": "Troubleshooting",
      "text": "| Problem | What to try |\n|---|---|\n| No models after installation | Check the target profile, confirm the plugin is enabled, restart DSH and check network connectivity. |\n| Thinking mode fails after a tool result with missing reasoning_content | Update the plugin; 0.5.3 restores the required assistant-history field, including empty reasoning. |\n| HTTP 429 | Retry later. If proxies are configured, inspect their status in Settings. |\n| HTTP 403 or 503 | Check for plugin updates and upstream service issues, then retry later. These errors do not trigger proxy failover. Report persistent problems. |\n| Tool calls fail | Check the **Diagnostic log** tab, or ask the agent to run `opencode_bridge_audit` for tool compatibility. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Troubleshooting",
      "text": "For bugs or feature requests, [choose an Issue form](https://github.com/Vikrant-Aleph/dsh-opencode-bridge/issues/new/choose) and fill in the requested versions, reproduction steps and expected/actual behavior. Redact logs first; do not include API keys, proxy passwords or private conversations."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development and technical documentation",
      "text": "<details>\n<summary>Develop and install from source</summary>\n\nRequires **Node.js ≥ 20.18.1** and pnpm. Node.js 22 or 24 LTS is recommended.\n\n```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/Vikrant-Aleph/dsh-opencode-bridge.git\ncd dsh-opencode-bridge\npnpm install\npnpm build\n\nBuild output is not committed to Git. To install a local build in DSH:\n\n```sh\npnpm pack\ndsh plugin --profile desktop add ./dsh-opencode-bridge-0.5.5.tgz\n```\n\n</details>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development and technical documentation",
      "text": "See the [technical documentation](TECHNICAL.md) ([中文](TECHNICAL.zh.md)) for implementation details, full configuration, testing and maintenance rules."
    },
    {
      "section": "Credits and license",
      "text": "Protocol research drew on the official OpenCode source and open-source projects including sub2api, 9router, hermes-oc-free-provider and cpa-plugin-opencodezen. Sources and comparison records are documented in the technical documentation.\n\nLicensed under [MIT](LICENSE)."
    }
  ],
